<SddModule keywords="module-decomposition, module-map, entity-inventory, dbc-contracts, ports-adapters, closed-world, file-structure, modes, add-module, refine-module, sdd-module" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Turn an approved `product` / `library` scope spec into a hierarchy of module specs: a
    closed-world entity inventory, an explicit public surface per entity, strict DbC contracts
    (Ports / Adapters / Services), and a designed file structure. Loaded lazily by the router;
    inherits the router core (language, dialogue, safeguard, diverge, no-narration, stateless) —
    not repeated here.

    Input — `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md`. Output — `specs/<scope>/<module>/<module>.spec.md`
    (nesting allowed) + the scope spec Module Map updated (append-only per module). Only for
    scope-type product / library.

    Out of scope: task tickets, BDD, execution plans, rules linkage — those belong to scaffold.
    The canonical worked example lives in the étalon (referenced at the write step), not inlined here.

    **Glossary.** Modes: initial · add-module · refine-module. Port = abstraction introduced ONLY on
    confirmed variability (≥2 impls) or an explicit test seam; a single impl without that is a
    Service, not a Port.
  </Mission>

