  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_INVALID_SCOPE_TYPE` | scope-type = infrastructure or interface — module-decomposition not applicable |
    | `H_SCOPE_SPEC_MISSING` | `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md` does not exist — run the scope flow first |
    | `H_INCOMPLETE_SCOPE_SPEC` | Scope spec missing required sections (Vision, Architecture, Golden DX) |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Module specs exist + mode verb absent + no Pivot Invalidation List |
    | `H_LOW_CONFIDENCE` | Confidence LOW at decomposition lock or final hierarchy |
    | `H_INVENTORY_NOT_APPROVED` | Entered the surface step without all-module inventories approved |
    | `H_REFINE_BREAKING_CHANGE_NO_LOG` | `refine-module` removes a public entity / weakens a postcondition without a Decision Log entry (`AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`) |
    | `H_REFINE_BREAKING_NO_IMPACT_LIST` | breaking `refine-module` without a Pivot Invalidation List enumerating consumer modules (`AX_REFINE_MODULE_PRESERVES_CONTRACTS`) |
    | `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE` | A module rule reference does not resolve to an existing file (and not `deferred`) |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator refused decomposition, inventory, surface, contract, structure, or final hierarchy |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Resolve scope, mode; gate scope-type.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md` (sole source per `AX_SPEC_IS_SOLE_SOURCE`). Missing →
        `H_SCOPE_SPEC_MISSING`; incomplete → `H_INCOMPLETE_SCOPE_SPEC`. scope-type must be
        product / library (`AX_SCOPE_TYPE_GATE`, else `H_INVALID_SCOPE_TYPE`). Mode per
        `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT` — initial / add-module / refine-module; the mode picked here
        controls step branching downstream (`AX_DIRECTIVE_MODE`). On `add-module` /
        `refine-module`, run `sdd-check --all specs/<scope>` first — an over-budget module
        (`SDD_MODULE_OVERSIZED` → decompose, `SDD_MODULE_SPEC_VERBOSE` → compress) is surfaced to the
        operator BEFORE new work, per `AX_HIERARCHICAL_SPECS`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_MODULE_MAP">
      <Goal>Lock module boundaries; update the scope Module Map.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Propose module boundaries along `AX_SEPARATION_OF_CONCERNS` (data/domain ↔ UI/presentation ↔
        infrastructure; a shared core only once ≥2 consumers need it); the operator confirms
        (`AX_MODULE_BOUNDARY_BY_OPERATOR`). Update
        the scope spec Module Map append-only (`AX_SCOPE_SPEC_MODULE_MAP_OWNERSHIP`) —
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-map-update.xml")`. `add-module`
        appends only (`AX_APPEND_ONLY_MODULE_ADD`). On `initial` this is the monolith→index migration
        (`AX_SCOPE_STAYS_THIN`): move entity / contract / file-level detail out of the scope spec into
        the new module specs, leaving the scope spec as the thin index (Module Map + composition Golden
        DX). Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_ENTITY_INVENTORY">
      <Goal>Closed-world inventory per module.</Goal>
      <Action>
        List every entity of the module — the complete world (`AX_CLOSED_WORLD_INVENTORY`); anything an
        execution agent adds beyond it is drift. Interview the operator via
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interview-protocol.directive.xml")`, extending
        its coverage map with the decomposition topics: «Пропущенная сущность» (what the inventory
        still misses) and «Бесхозная ответственность» (a responsibility no listed entity owns).
        Size the interview to the confirmed `scale:` from the session file
        (`AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`). Keep evidence separated per `AX_EVIDENCE_HYGIENE`: entities
        named by the scope spec are facts; entities inferred during the interview stay hypotheses
        until the operator confirms them.
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/entity-inventory-format.xml")`. If a
        module's inventory outgrows cohesion (too many entities / unrelated responsibility clusters),
        PROPOSE sub-module decomposition here per `AX_HIERARCHICAL_SPECS` (diverge-before-recommend;
        the operator decides) — do not silently let one module absorb a sub-system. All module
        inventories must be approved before the surface step (else `H_INVENTORY_NOT_APPROVED`).
        Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_ENTITY_SURFACE">
      <Goal>Public surface per entity.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Define each entity's public surface (`AX_ENTITY_SURFACE_COMPLETENESS`). No consumer → no entity
        (`AX_CONSUMER_DRIVEN`): an entity without a confirmed v1 consumer is dropped or `deferred`.
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/entity-surface-format.xml")`. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_CONTRACTS_DBC">
      <Goal>DbC contract per entity.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Preconditions / postconditions / invariants per entity — written textual and
        language-agnostic per `AX_CONTRACTS_TEXTUAL_AGNOSTIC` (target-language code appears only in
        usage examples). A Port is introduced ONLY on confirmed
        variability or a test seam (`AX_PORTS_AND_ABSTRACTIONS_DISCIPLINE`) — Port-vs-Service is a
        design choice, so apply `AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND` (do not default to Port). Each abstraction
        carries its justification (`AX_CONTEXT_TO_CONTRACT`); runtime backing is stated per contract
        (`AX_RUNTIME_BACKING_IN_CONTRACTS`).
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/dbc-contracts.xml")`.
        Close the step with two checks before presenting:
        1. Every module / entity / Port in the contracts carries a confirmed v1 consumer or
           near-term variability (`AX_YAGNI_OVERENGINEERING_GUARD`).
        2. Every public option / flag / policy the scope spec mentions is bound to a concrete
           Port / Adapter contract or explicitly marked `deferred / not consumed in v1` with a
           pointer to the task or version that activates it (`AX_NO_SILENT_OPTION_DROP`).
        STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FILE_STRUCTURE">
      <Goal>Design the file structure.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Repo layout; physically split `ports/` (or `contracts/`) from `adapters/` (or `impl/`). No God
        objects, file size ≤ 1500 lines (`AX_MODULARITY_LIMITS`); single grep namespace
        (`AX_NAMESPACE_NAMING`). STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_FINAL_HIERARCHY">
      <Goal>Emit the module spec hierarchy.</Goal>
      <Action>
        On `initial` / `add-module`, for each new module create its skeleton via
        `sdd-new module --scope <scope> --module <module>` — it never overwrites and prints the
        section manifest (which sections are REQUIRED and what to fill); on `refine-module` the file
        already exists, edit it in place, skip `sdd-new`. Content guidance per
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-spec-structure.xml")`. Assemble
        each `specs/<scope>/<module>/<module>.spec.md` to it; link back to `../../<scope>.spec.md`;
        reconcile the scope Module Map. In `pivot` / breaking `refine-module` also
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/pivot-formats.xml")`
        (`AX_REFINE_MODULE_PRESERVES_CONTRACTS`, else `H_REFINE_BREAKING_CHANGE_NO_LOG`). For a breaking
        `refine-module`, derive consumer modules from the reverse edges of the module graph (siblings whose
        `Inter-Module Dependencies` declares `--> this-module`) and emit a Pivot Invalidation List in the module spec — else
        `H_REFINE_BREAKING_NO_IMPACT_LIST`. When a module needs rules beyond the scope-wide
        baseline, fill Module Rules Additions in the Handoff section per `AX_RULE_ACTIVATION`
        (shortlist + considered-skips, operator locks the list; architecture / infra rules get the
        per-axiom walk-through); every referenced rule file must resolve, else
        `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`. Before writing, run the self-check pass per
        `AX_ARTIFACT_STYLE_SELF_CHECK`. Write in review-state per `AX_SPEC_LIFECYCLE` — prepend a
        `CHANGE_MANIFEST` (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/change-manifest.xml")`) and
        mark changed lines `✚`/`~` (greenfield → manifest only, no per-line marks); compress folds it to
        master downstream after the change ships. Then run
        `sdd-check --all specs/<scope>` (anchor balance + required sections + links + size budget:
        `SDD_MODULE_OVERSIZED` / `SDD_MODULE_SPEC_VERBOSE`) and resolve or consciously defer any finding
        per `AX_CLOSE_WITH_INTEGRITY_CHECK`. Then
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/review-lifecycle.directive.xml")` — internal critic →
        publish (MR) → external review → compress + merge on approval. Only after the spec merges to master,
        hand off to scaffold (`AX_HANDOFF_TO_TASK_SCAFFOLDING`). Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

